TrialBox: third-party notices
=============================

This file lists the third-party material that the TrialBox demo image (demo/Dockerfile) ships, with the
version, the licence and what the licence asks of us (attribution text, notice, conditions). The console shows
it at /about. The demo image copies this folder (trialbox/) minus .dockerignore, installs the Python packages of
deploy/requirements.lock, fetches two fonts (tools/fetch_fonts.py) and, when tools/fetch_jvm_deps.sh has run
before the build, carries the CQL translator jars in .cache/jvm/cql-translator/lib.

Every patient in the demo is synthetic. The code lists below are demo subsets, not complete releases.

Scope: this file is written from the licence register, docs/licences/register.csv (cards T-617a and T-617b,
finding STD-044, D-342). `python -m tools.licence_register --check` fails the build when a shipped data file has
no register row.
Open items are listed in section 9. tests/unit/test_notice.py fails when a vocabulary folder the image ships
is not named in section 8.

Sections: 1 code systems and vocabularies; 2 FHIR and data-model material; 3 clinical scores and catalogue
sources; 4 public data sets; 5 Java libraries (CQL translator); 6 fonts and JavaScript; 7 Python packages and
the base image; 8 shipped vocabulary folders; 9 open items.


