3. CLINICAL SCORES AND CATALOGUE SOURCES
===============================================================================================================

catalogue/scores/*.yaml hold scoring formulas with the published source cited in each file (source and licence
fields). No licensed questionnaire text is shipped (catalogue/README.md). Two instruments carry conditions:
  MoCA: copyright of MoCA Test Inc.; administering it needs training and certification; TrialBox stores the
    score only (catalogue/scores/moca_adjusted.yaml), https://mocacognition.com
  PHQ-9: developed by Drs. Robert L. Spitzer, Janet B.W. Williams, Kurt Kroenke and colleagues, with an
    educational grant from Pfizer Inc. No permission required to reproduce, translate, display or distribute.

services/criteria_compiler/ir_extract/negation_scope.py adapts the English negation cue words of medspaCy 1.3.1's
ConText rules (resources/en/context_rules.json; https://pypi.org/project/medspacy/1.3.1/), themselves from pyConText
and NegEx (Harkema H et al., J Biomed Inform 2009;42(5):839-51). MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 medspacy: the full
notice is in that file's header. The Japanese and Chinese cues are TrialBox's own.


